WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:16.588
The children and Mrs. Darling were comforting Nana with pats and cuddles.

2
00:00:16.589 --> 00:00:23.085
Nana's stomach was upset from drinking Mr. Darling's medicine.

3
00:00:23.086 --> 00:00:27.236
"It was only a joke," Mr. Darling said.

4
00:00:27.237 --> 00:00:32.223
It was clear that nobody had any sympathy for him, and this upset him.

5
00:00:32.224 --> 00:00:38.679
"All you care about is that dog. What about my feelings?" he shouted.

6
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:43.691
Then he said, "The proper place for a dog is tied up in the yard!"

7
00:00:43.692 --> 00:00:48.838
To prove his point, Mr. Darling dragged Nana from the nursery.

8
00:00:48.839 --> 00:00:53.720
He pulled her outside and chained her to a tree in the backyard.

9
00:00:53.721 --> 00:00:58.252
Suddenly ashamed, he sat down on the back steps and cried.

10
00:00:58.253 --> 00:01:02.865
He knew he had made a mistake, but Mr. Darling could not give in.

11
00:01:02.866 --> 00:01:07.281
He couldn't face his family if he had to admit that he was wrong.

12
00:01:07.282 --> 00:01:13.830
So, that night, Nana was left in the backyard, away from the nursery.

13
00:01:13.831 --> 00:01:19.383
Mrs. Darling put the kids to bed. They could all hear Nana barking outside.

14
00:01:19.384 --> 00:01:24.783
John whimpered, "Poor Nana. She sounds so unhappy."

15
00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:30.407
But Wendy was wiser. "That is not Nana's unhappy bark.

16
00:01:30.408 --> 00:01:34.104
It's how she barks when she smells danger."

17
00:01:34.105 --> 00:01:38.346
Mrs. Darling checked the nursery window to make sure it was properly shut.

18
00:01:38.347 --> 00:01:44.294
"Oh, how I wish I weren't going to a dinner party tonight!" she thought to herself.

19
00:01:44.295 --> 00:01:50.588
She was worried about leaving the children in the nursery without Nana to watch them.

20
00:01:50.589 --> 00:01:55.586
"The night lights will keep you from harm," she told the children.

21
00:01:55.587 --> 00:02:00.385
She tucked each child into bed. She sang each a song.

22
00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:06.332
She kissed them good night on their eyelids and, with that, she left the nursery.

23
00:02:06.333 --> 00:02:10.609
Then Mr. and Mrs. Darling went out into the night.

24
00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:12.834
They didn't have far to go.

25
00:02:12.835 --> 00:02:18.240
The dinner party was at Number 27, only a few yards away from their house.

26
00:02:18.241 --> 00:02:22.929
It had been snowing, and they were the only people in the street.

27
00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:27.761
The stars shone down on the soft white covering of snow and on the couple.

28
00:02:27.762 --> 00:02:38.405
But as soon as the door of Number 27 closed behind them, the stars, who were friends of Peter Pan, whispered, "Go now, Peter!"

29
00:02:38.406 --> 00:02:43.453
Back in the nursery, Wendy, John, and Michael had fallen asleep.

30
00:02:43.454 --> 00:02:47.936
A bright light darted from one dresser drawer to another.

31
00:02:47.937 --> 00:02:50.600
It was not really a light, though.

32
00:02:50.601 --> 00:02:56.951
When it rested for a moment, you could see it was a fairy no larger than a hand.

33
00:02:56.952 --> 00:02:59.848
The fairy's name was Tinker Bell.

34
00:02:59.849 --> 00:03:04.848
A perfect miniature figure, she was beautifully dressed in a tiny leaf.

35
00:03:04.849 --> 00:03:09.331
She had found a way into the nursery to look for Peter's shadow.

36
00:03:09.332 --> 00:03:14.965
Suddenly the window blew open, and Peter flew into the nursery.

37
00:03:14.966 --> 00:03:19.735
"Tinker Bell," he called softly, "where are you?"

38
00:03:19.736 --> 00:03:26.516
He had carried the fairy part of the way from Neverland, and her fairy dust was still all over his hands.

39
00:03:26.517 --> 00:03:30.895
"Come and help me find my shadow!" Peter said.

40
00:03:30.896 --> 00:03:36.380
The ring of a tiny bell answered him. This was Tinker Bell's fairy language.

41
00:03:36.381 --> 00:03:45.236
When Tinker Bell explained that his shadow was in the dresser, Peter rummaged through all the drawers, spilling everything all over the floor.

42
00:03:45.237 --> 00:03:49.124
He made a terrible mess, but he didn't notice.

43
00:03:49.125 --> 00:03:54.870
He also didn't notice that he accidentally locked Tinker Bell in one of the drawers.

44
00:03:54.871 --> 00:03:59.602
Finally, Peter found his shadow. He was delighted.

45
00:03:59.603 --> 00:04:03.155
But how could he attach it to himself again?

46
00:04:03.156 --> 00:04:06.648
Peter put the shadow on the floor and lay down on it.

47
00:04:06.649 --> 00:04:09.155
But it wouldn't stick to his body.

48
00:04:09.156 --> 00:04:12.942
Next he tried to glue it on with soap from the bathroom.

49
00:04:12.943 --> 00:04:23.533
But this didn't work either. Frustrated, Peter sat down and cried.
